at least version of this game, and in the Gillam booklet, but the primary
source below quotes the move order as given in the main line.}) 3. Nf3 Nf6 4.
Nc3 e6 5. e3 Nbd7 6. Bd3 Be7 7. O-O O-O 8. e4 dxe4 9. Nxe4 b6 10. Qe2 Bb7 11.
Rd1 Qc7 12. Bg5 c5 13. Bh4 Rac8 14. Bg3 Qc6 15. d5 exd5 16. Nxf6+ Bxf6 17. cxd5
{Source: Staffordshire Advertiser, 18 January 1930} (17. cxd5 {premature
resignation: Winter thought that, after} Qa4 18. Bb5 {won a piece, overlooking
that} Qg4 {defended the threatened knight (BCM, Feb 1930, p56)}) 1-0

